// RUN: check
// COMPILE-FAIL
// EXPECT-EXIT: 65
// CHECK-ERR: auto requires an initializer.
//
// Chapter 02 coverage: `auto` infers its type from the initializer, so it
// has no meaning without one. Unlike bare scalar declarations (`int a;`,
// legal but unread-before-assign per definite assignment), `auto x;` is
// rejected outright at declaration time.

int main() {
  auto x;
  return x;
}
